    x([K,2,'en'],'M39 p. 292 (pdf 185L)','English (Douay) to follow the Latin lesson: it had Mic 7:14b "in the midst of Carmel: they shall feed in Basan and Galaad" and 7:16b "they shall put the hand upon the mouth, their ears shall be deaf", which the Missal does not read, and lacked "Dómine Deus noster" at the beginning and end',
      new='O Lord our God, feed thy people with thy rod, the flock of thy inheritance, them that dwell alone in the forest, according to the days of old. The nations shall see, and shall be confounded at all their strength. Who is a God like to thee, who takest away iniquity, and passest by the sin of the remnant of thy inheritance? he will send his fury in no more, because he delighteth in mercy. He will turn again, and have mercy on us: he will put away our iniquities: and he will cast all our sins into the bottom of the sea. Thou wilt perform the truth of Jacob, the mercy to Abraham: which thou hast sworn to our fathers from the days of old, O Lord our God.')
    x([K,3,'la'],'M39 p. 293 (pdf 185R)',SC,subs=[('Jerúsalem: nolíte','Jerúsalem: Nolíte'),('Loquímini veritátem unusquísque','Loquímini veritátem, unusquísque'),('córdibus vestris, et juraméntum','córdibus vestris: et juraméntum'),('diligátis: ómnia enim','diligátis: Omnia enim'),('præcláras: veritátem','præcláras: Veritátem')])
    x([K,3,'ref'],'M39 p. 293 (pdf 185R)','the lesson ends at v. 19 ("Dicit Dóminus exercítuum" closes it; v. 20 is not read); masses.js and the St Dominic Missal (p. 581) give 8: 14-19',new='Zacharias 8: 14-19')
    x([K,3,'en'],'M39 p. 293 (pdf 185R)','English ran into v. 20 ("until people come, and dwell in many cities,"), lacked the opening "Factum est verbum Dómini ad me, dicens" and the ending "Dicit Dóminus exercítuum", and had "For" (Vulgate "Quia"), which the Latin lacks',
      new='In those days: The word of the Lord came to me, saying: Thus saith the Lord of hosts: As I purposed to afflict you, when your fathers had provoked me to wrath, saith the Lord, And I had no mercy: so turning again I have thought in these days to do good to the house of Juda, and Jerusalem: fear not. These then are the things, which you shall do: Speak ye truth every one to his neighbour: judge ye truth and judgment of peace in your gates. And let none of you imagine evil in your hearts against his friend: and love not a false oath: for all these are the things that I hate, saith the Lord. And the word of the Lord of hosts came to me, saying: Thus saith the Lord of hosts: The fast of the fourth month, and the fast of the fifth, and the fast of the seventh, and the fast of the tenth shall be to the house of Juda, joy, and gladness, and great solemnities: only love ye truth and peace, saith the Lord of hosts.')
    x([K,4,'la'],'M39 p. 293 (pdf 185R)',SC+'; restores the lines dropped by the 1933 OCR: "Flamma autem effundebátur super fornácem cúbitis quadragínta novem: et erúpit, et incéndit quos réperit juxta fornácem de Chaldǽis, minístros regis, qui eam incendébant." (as in Pent0s, Adv3s, Quad1s)',
      new='In diébus illis: Angelus Dómini descéndit cum Azaría, et sóciis ejus in fornácem: et excússit flammam ignis de fornáce, et fecit médium fornácis quasi ventum roris flantem. Flamma autem effundebátur super fornácem cúbitis quadragínta novem: et erúpit, et incéndit quos réperit juxta fornácem de Chaldǽis, minístros regis, qui eam incendébant. Et non tétigit eos omníno ignis, neque contristávit, nec quidquam moléstiæ íntulit. Tunc hi tres quasi ex uno ore laudábant, et glorificábant, et benedicébant Deum in fornáce, dicéntes.')
    x([K,4,'ref'],'M39 p. 293 (pdf 185R)','with the restored lines the lesson reads Dan 3:47-51 (as masses.js, Adv3s and Quad1s)',new='Daniel 3: 47-51')
    x([K,4,'en'],'M39 p. 293 (pdf 185R)','the English lacked the lines restored to the Latin (Dan 3:47-48); the Missal\'s "minístros regis, qui eam incendébant" is not in the Vulgate v. 48: AI translation of that sentence, labelled (RULINGS 27 Nov 23:00); same English as Pent0s (same Latin, p. 256)',
      new='In those days: The angel of the Lord went down with Azarias and his companions into the furnace: and he drove the flame of the fire out of the furnace, And made the midst of the furnace like the blowing of a wind bringing dew. And the flame streamed out above the furnace nine and forty cubits: and it broke forth, and burned those of the Chaldeans whom it found near the furnace, the king’s servants who were heating it. [AI translation of the Missal’s Latin for this sentence.] And the fire touched them not at all, nor troubled them, nor did them any harm. Then these three as with one mouth praised, and glorified, and blessed God in the furnace, saying.')
    x([K,5,'la'],'M39 p. 294 (pdf 186L)',SC,subs=[('supérque eam erant chérubim','supérque eam erant Chérubim'),('ita compósitis, in prióri','ita compósitis: in prióri'),('consummántes: in secúndo','consummántes: In secúndo'),('significánte Spíritu sancto,','significánte Spíritu Sancto,'),('habénte statum: quæ parábola','habénte statum. Quæ parábola'),('per próprium sánguinem','per próprium Sánguinem'),('perféctius tabernáculum, non manufáctum','perféctius tabernáculum non manufáctum')])
    x([K,6,'la'],'M39 p. 295 (pdf 186R)',SC,subs=[('invénio: succíde ergo illam: ut quid','invénio: Succíde ergo illam: Ut quid'),('stércora, et si quidem fécerit fructum: sin autem','stércora: Et si quidem fécerit fructum: Sin autem'),('curásset Jesus, dicébat','curásset Jesus: dicébat'),('operári: in his','operári: In his'),('alligávit Sátanas','alligávit sátanas'),('ejus: et omnis','ejus: Et omnis')])
