# ---- AscVig (In Vigilia Ascensionis Domini, M39 pp. 233-235, pdf 155R-156R): the site had the Roman orations (Divinum Officium Pasc5-3)
WAV='the Missal\'s own prayer of this Mass (the site had the Roman one, src "Tempora/Pasc5-3": "Deus, a quo bona cuncta" / "Súscipe, Dómine, fidélium preces" / "Tríbue nobis, Dómine, cœléstis mensæ"), as printed; conclusion type as printed (Rubr. gen. XI.2, p. 52); English: St Dominic Missal 1959 pp. 461-464 (pdf 485-488, read on the page images), conclusion expanded'
o('AscVig','or','M39 p. 234 (pdf 156L)','Præsta, quǽsumus, omnípotens Deus: ut nostræ mentis inténtio, quo solemnitátis ventúræ gloriósus auctor ingréssus est, semper inténdat; et quo fide pergit, conversatióne pervéniat: Per eúmdem Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum Fílium tuum; qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus: per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.',why=WAV+' ("Per eúmdem")')
x(['AscVig','or',1],'DM 1959 p. 461 (pdf 485)',WAV,file=O,new='Grant, we beseech You, almighty God, that the bent of our minds may always tend where the glorious author of the coming solemnity has entered; and attain by holy living that towards which it journeys by faith: through the same Lord Jesus Christ, Your Son, who lives and reigns with You in the unity of the Holy Spirit, God, world without end.')
o('AscVig','se','M39 p. 235 (pdf 156R)','Sacrifícium, Dómine, pro Fílii tui súpplices venerábili, quam prævenímus, Ascensióne deférimus: præsta quǽsumus, ut et nos per ipsum his commérciis sacrosánctis ad cæléstia consurgámus. Qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus: per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.',why=WAV+' ("Qui tecum")')
x(['AscVig','se',1],'DM 1959 p. 463 (pdf 487)',WAV,file=O,new='We, Your humble servants, offer to You, O Lord, this sacrifice in honor of the glorious ascension of Your Son which we now anticipate; grant, we beseech You, that through Him we may, by means of these most holy offices, rise to the things of heaven: who lives and reigns with You in the unity of the Holy Spirit, God, world without end.')
o('AscVig','pc','M39 p. 235 (pdf 156R)','Tríbue, quǽsumus Dómine: ut per hæc sacraménta, quæ súmpsimus, illuc tendat nostræ devotiónis afféctus; quo tecum est nostra substántia, Jesus Christus Dóminus noster: Qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus: per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.',why=WAV+' ("Qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte")')
x(['AscVig','pc',1],'DM 1959 p. 464 (pdf 488)',WAV,file=O,new='Grant, we beseech You, O Lord, that through this sacrament which we have received our hearts may tend where Jesus Christ our Lord in our human nature dwells: who lives and reigns with You in the unity of the Holy Spirit, God, world without end.')
x(['AscVig','src'],'M39 pp. 234-235 (pdf 156L-R)','source of the corrected orations',file=O,new='Missale O.P. (1939), p. 234-235 (In Vigilia Ascensionis Domini); English St Dominic Missal (1959), pp. 461-464')
x(['AscVig',0,'la'],'M39 p. 234 (pdf 156L)',SC+' ("super omnes" for the garbled "superpónes")',subs=[('in altum, captívam','in altum captívam'),('superpónes cælos','super omnes cælos'),('quidem apóstolos, quosdam autem prophétas, álios vero evangelístas','quidem Apóstolos, quosdam autem Prophétas, álios vero Evangelístas'),('et doctóres, ad consummatiónem','et doctóres ad consummatiónem')])
x(['AscVig',1,'la'],'M39 pp. 234-235 (pdf 156L-R)',SC+' ("apud te" for the garbled "apud e")',
  new='In illo témpore: Sublevátis Jesus óculis in cælum, dixit: Pater, venit hora, clarífica Fílium tuum, ut Fílius tuus claríficet te: Sicut dedísti ei potestátem omnis carnis, ut omne, quod dedísti ei, det eis vitam ætérnam. Hæc est autem vita ætérna: ut cognóscant te, solum Deum verum, et quem misísti Jesum Christum. Ego te clarificávi super terram: opus consummávi, quod dedísti mihi ut fáciam: Et nunc clarífica me tu Pater apud temetípsum, claritáte, quam hábui, priúsquam mundus esset, apud te. Manifestávi nomen tuum homínibus, quos dedísti mihi de mundo: Tui erant, et mihi eos dedísti: et sermónem tuum servavérunt. Nunc cognovérunt quia ómnia, quæ dedísti mihi, abs te sunt: quia verba, quæ dedísti mihi, dedi eis: Et ipsi accepérunt, et cognovérunt vere quia a te exívi, et credidérunt quia tu me misísti. Ego pro eis rogo: Non pro mundo rogo, sed pro his, quos dedísti mihi: quia tui sunt: Et mea ómnia tua sunt, et tua mea sunt: et clarificátus sum in eis: Et jam non sum in mundo, et hi in mundo sunt, et ego ad te vénio.')
x(['AscVig',1,'en'],'M39 p. 235 (pdf 156R)','English ran into Jn 17:11b ("Holy Father, keep them …"), which the Latin (ending "et ego ad te vénio") lacks',subs=[(' Holy Father, keep them in thy name whom thou has given me; that they may be one, as we also are.','')])
